course: dictionary
lesson: 15631
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and tempo is one of them. Context tells you which meaning is meant, and the other words in the sentence are your clues. «The band played the song at a fast tempo.» The clues are band and song, so tempo means the speed of the music.
explain: «The tempo of the game picked up in the second half.» There are no instruments here, but the clues are game and picked up. Tempo means the speed or pace at which something happens. Ask yourself: is the sentence about music, or about how fast something goes? That question sorts out the meaning.
explain: Musicians use Italian words for tempo: allegro (fast), andante (walking pace) and largo (slow). They count beats per minute, and a metronome clicks at the speed they choose so they can keep to the tempo.
fact: Tempo is a noun. Its plural can be tempos or tempi.
fact: «Tempo» means the speed of a piece of music: fast, slow or in between.
fact: «Tempo» also means the speed or pace at which something happens, like a game or life in a city.
fact: In music, «allegro» means fast, «andante» means walking pace, and «largo» means slow.
fact: A metronome clicks at a set number of beats per minute, so musicians can keep the same tempo.
exercise: «The drummer kept a steady tempo all through the song.» What does tempo mean here? | The loudest part of the song | The colour of the drum | *The speed of the music | The name of the band
exercise: «The tempo of life in the city is very fast.» What does tempo mean here? | Something you can eat | *The pace at which things happen | A kind of music | A type of bus
exercise: Which Italian word in the lesson means slow in music? | andante | *largo | allegro
test: «The team raised the tempo in the second half.» What does this suggest? | They stopped playing altogether | *They started playing faster | They changed their shirts | They sang a song
test: Lily says tempo only means music. Which sentence shows she is wrong? | *«The tempo of the match was very fast.» | «The piano was in tune.» | «The song had a happy chorus.» | «The orchestra played loudly.»
exam: «The conductor waved her arms and the orchestra changed tempo to a slow largo.» What is the best meaning of tempo here? | The shape of the conductor's baton | The name of the orchestra | The number of players in the orchestra | *The speed of the music
